package spawn

// Verification status (26.3 reference, see testdata/ and refdata/).
//
// Oracle setup. Probes in tools/refprobe/java/kremenmc/probe/spawn boot an
// in-process GameTestServer (flat test world) in .refcache/26.3, build a
// scene from a script (testdata/scenes/*.txt, generated by
// testdata/gen/scenes.py), freeze ticking, dump everything the engine reads
// (blocks, sky/block light, local brightness, biomes, heightmaps, ticking
// chunks, entities, env values) and run operations with the level random
// replaced (reflection on Level.random) by a recording RandomSource. Spawn
// predicates and callbacks emit markers. The Go tests replay each operation
// on the dump with a scripted rng.Source that must see the same calls with
// the same arguments in the same order; the full logs must be equal.
// Reference entry points: NaturalSpawner.spawnCategoryForPosition /
// spawnCategoryForChunk / spawnForChunk / spawnMobsForChunkGeneration /
// createState / getFilteredSpawningCategories, SpawnState.canSpawn and
// afterSpawn (reflective), SpawnPlacements.isSpawnPositionOk /
// checkSpawnRules (through a ServerLevelAccessor proxy to override the sea
// level), Mob.getWalkTargetValue / checkSpawnRules / checkSpawnObstruction /
// checkDespawn, BaseSpawner.serverTick, DifficultyInstance, plus static
// tables (MobCategory, SpawnPlacements, EntityType, BlockState).
//
// Verified exactly against the reference:
//   - MobCategory values, NaturalSpawner constants, SPAWNING_CATEGORIES,
//     BaseSpawner defaults, spawn-related game rule ids (refdata/static.txt).
//   - Entity table for all registry entries: category, summonable, far
//     spawn, fire immunity, size, peaceful flag, placement type, heightmap;
//     per-mob cluster size, group limit, removeWhenFarAway and
//     requiresCustomPersistence of fresh instances; dangerous block states.
//   - Block table for every state: redstone conductor, full collision,
//     signal source, air, liquid, light emission/dampening, fluid,
//     land-pathfindable, and the isValidSpawn class per entity type. State
//     and entity IDs match internal/data (tables_test.go).
//   - DifficultyInstance (700 vectors).
//   - SpawnPlacements.isSpawnPositionOk and checkSpawnRules (draw sequence
//     and result) for all 57 mobs in vanilla biome/structure spawn lists over
//     32 floor/content cells x 4 light situations (open, roofed, lit, cave)
//     in plains night/day, swamp, snowy+thunder and peaceful, plus water and
//     lava pools at 11-37 depths in 5 biomes (17k cases).
//   - getWalkTargetValue, Mob.checkSpawnRules, checkSpawnObstruction and
//     the light helpers for 20 representative mobs (3.5k cases).
//   - spawnCategoryForPosition (196 cases) and spawnCategoryForChunk (144):
//     pack size, wander, nearest player and world-spawn distance, ticking
//     chunks, weighted selection, count providers, reduce_water_ambient,
//     placement/rules/collision, yaw, walk target, obstruction, cluster and
//     group limits (incl. solitary tropical fish), with real spawns of 17
//     types.
//   - Spawn potential (soul sand valley charges, 96 chunk attempts).
//   - spawnMobsForChunkGeneration draw sequence in the flat test world
//     (96 calls; the spawn_mobs game rule gates it) and the chunk
//     generation seed: yaws of creatures saved by a real dedicated server
//     (separate JVM, seed 12345) all occur in the stream of ChunkGenSeed
//     (WorldgenRandom over legacy, setDecorationSeed(seed, minX, minZ)),
//     and their x/z are integer or clamped by the entity width (no +0.5).
//   - checkDespawn: 180 cases over 5 types, 6 distances, idle times,
//     named/persistent (persistent mobs keep noActionTime).
//   - BaseSpawner.serverTick: delay countdown/reroll, positions, rules,
//     max nearby, finalize, spawn count (6 runs, 30-60 ticks each).
//   - finalizeSpawn draw sequences for Mob base (all types declaring it
//     only on Mob), AgeableMob, tropical fish, sheep (classic colors),
//     cow/pig/chicken (data-driven variant + sound variant), horse, squid,
//     glow squid, dolphin, spider (non-jockey, non-hard path). Results
//     (colors, attributes) are rolled but their values are not compared.
//
// Implemented from documentation / reasoning only (not oracle-verified):
//   - LocalMobCapCalculator (DefaultPlayersNear; the reference also needs
//     the chunk in the player ticket range), category gating in
//     ServerChunkCache (TickGates: persistent categories every 400 ticks,
//     spawn_monsters/peaceful), chunk shuffling (ShuffleChunks), TickNatural.
//   - Structure spawn overrides and the nether fortress list (parsing
//     verified only through Go tests; no structure exists in the test world).
//   - Rules in other dimensions (nether ambient light 0.1 path is exercised
//     only through the formula), spawner custom spawn rules, spawner NBT
//     positions, trial spawners (stub), special spawners (stubs).
//   - finalizeSpawn of zombies, skeletons, piglins, drowned, illagers,
//     wolves, cats, frogs, rabbits, foxes, villagers and a few more
//     (finalize_gear.go): outcome rates match the reference
//     (TestFinalizeGearRates) but the draw sequences are not known. Other
//     types not listed above: Base only.
//   - Halloween is treated as October 31 (SpecialDates.HALLOWEEN = --10-31;
//     isHalloween() false on 10-28).
